BT /F2 18 Tf 48 770 Td (Kafka and event ordering) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 737 Td (21. What events and topics are used?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 715 Td (The main types are OrderCreated, StockReserved and StockRejected. Order events use) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 699 Td (orders.events; completion events use inventory.events. Envelopes contain an event ID,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 683 Td (type, order ID, SKU, quantity, optional stock and UTC occurrence time. Failed records) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 667 Td (can be sent to the corresponding .DLT topic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 637 Td (22. Why use SKU as the Kafka key?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 615 Td (A SKU key routes events for the same product to the same partition within a topic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 599 Td (Kafka preserves partition order; it does not guarantee a global order across) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 583 Td (partitions or across topics. SQL row locking still protects stock updates.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 553 Td (23. What is a consumer group?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 531 Td (Consumers with the same group ID share a topic's partitions. Different groups each) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 515 Td (receive their own view of the events. Inventory and Notifications use separate groups) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 499 Td (so both can receive order events. With three partitions, at most three consumers in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 483 Td (group can actively read that topic at once.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 453 Td (24. What if StockReserved arrives before OrderCreated?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 431 Td (This can happen because the two events are on different topics. Analytics can create a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 415 Td (projection from the completion event. A later OrderCreated fills in creation time) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 399 Td (without resetting the final status to pending. Order counting also deduplicates by) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 383 Td (order ID, even if a creation event is repeated under a new event ID.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 353 Td (25. What are retries and dead-letter topics for?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 331 Td (Unhandled processing failures get up to three retries at 500 ms intervals, then go to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 315 Td (the source topic's .DLT with diagnostic headers. Examples include malformed envelopes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 299 Td (or unknown SKUs. A failed DLT publication must not be treated as successful recovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 283 Td (Fix the cause before replaying valid records with their original identity.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48 253 Td (26. How are stale stock snapshots handled?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 231 Td (The analytics stock projection uses the smaller of its existing and incoming stock) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 215 Td (values. This works because the current model only deducts stock. If restocking is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 199 Td (introduced, this rule would be wrong; I would use a version or sequence per SKU to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 48 183 Td (reject older updates while allowing legitimate increases.) Tj ET
